            "report": "# Implementer report\n\nImplemented task `csv-records` in `csv_records.py` using only Python standard-library csv and io modules. Verified starting HEAD matched expected base `b68fa11a9fceb2cf53227d257f7494d9d9307452`.\n\nThe reader preserves quoted commas and embedded newlines, trims headers and cells, rejects empty or duplicate normalized headers, validates each row width before dictionary construction, and returns an empty list for blank or header-only input.\n\nValidation:\n- Before implementation: `python3 -m unittest -v test_csv_records` failed (4 tests, 7 errors from the NotImplementedError stub).\n- After implementation: the same command passed all 4 tests, covering quoted, headers, ragged, and empty requirements.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\nSelf-review: inspected the complete implementation diff. Header validation precedes record construction; row-width validation prevents zip from silently dropping cells. StringIO with newline=\"\" lets the csv module handle embedded newlines. Only csv_records.py is included in the implementation commit; the Plan and protected tests were not edited. Required evaluation artifacts remain in ignored .eval/. No external dependencies, network access, delegation, or push were used. No outstanding issues found within the declared scope.\n",
